relation_to_broader_scientific_literatur.value:
The key contributions of the paper build upon prior research in graph OOD. For instance, the authors extend the works [1-3], all of which focus on solving the distribution shift issue on graphs. Note that the contributions of this paper are quite novel, addressing a gap in the literature that has not been fully explored before.

[1] Discovering invariant rationales for graph neural networks, ICLR 2022;  
[2] Does invariant graph learning via environment augmentation learn invariance? NeurIPS 2023;  
[3] Joint learning of label and environment causal independence for graph out-of-distribution generalization, NeurIPS 2023.

